/target
**/*.rs.bk

# The fuzz workspace has its own target directory, because it is deliberately not a
# member of the root workspace: `cargo-fuzz` builds with libFuzzer and a sanitizer,
# which needs nightly, and making it a member would force the pinned stable toolchain
# that builds the runner and its contract fixtures to be a nightly too.
fuzz/target

# A fuzz corpus is built up by running the fuzzer, which produces thousands of files
# nobody reads; CI caches it instead. A crashing input is uploaded as an artefact.
# A *seed* worth keeping is committed by hand under `fuzz/<target>/seeds/`, with the
# reason it is interesting, and that directory is tracked.
fuzz/corpus
fuzz/artifacts
fuzz/coverage

# The lock file is committed on purpose. An unpinned dependency tree would let a
# conformance verdict change without a commit, which is the drift this project
# exists to make visible.
Cargo.lock.orig

# A contract fixture built outside the workspace — `measurable-token` declares its own
# `[workspace]` so that it can be compiled for WebAssembly — writes its build output
# beside itself.
#
# The artefact that is *measured* is the copy under `fixtures/wasm/`, and that one is
# committed on purpose: the runner's `.wasm` target can only be tested against a real
# compilation, and a suite that first had to build one would not run on a checkout that
# is only reading. `scripts/build-fixture-wasm.sh` refreshes the copy, and CI rebuilds
# it and fails if the committed one differs, so a committed artefact cannot go stale
# without a red job.
fixtures/contracts/*/target

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.DS_Store

# A developer's own network credentials are never tracked. The documented form
# for local configuration is `estamora.local.toml`.
estamora.local.toml
*.local.toml
.env
.env.*

# Insta snapshots are reviewed and committed; the pending directory is not.
**/*.snap.new
**/.insta-pending

# The Soroban test host writes a JSON snapshot of ledger state beside the tests
# that use it. It is host state, not an artefact of this repository: two hosts at
# the same ledger point produce it, its contents are an SDK implementation
# detail, and committing it would make an SDK upgrade look like a change to the
# runner.
test_snapshots/
